ff structure. The payoff table is clear: cooperate yields -2, one defects -5, one defects and the other cooperates 0, and both defect is -4. I'm aligning this with the \"Twin Prisoner's Dilemma\" analysis from the researcher's essay, where the high correlation of decisions between identical agents is highlighted. EDT is indicating that cooperation is the preferred choice. Also, exploring section 5.2 to understand why algorithmic self-similarity cannot be ignored.\n\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":1}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8738,"completion_tokens":535,"total_tokens":9273,"cost":0.00855975,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00855975,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0065535,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00200625},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":534,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}